concepts/skins.content:
Skins System

Appearance customization system for FDE Desktop with two independent axes: color skins and window control styles. Both are selected separately and can be combined freely.
Overview
The system separates two concerns that were previously coupled:




















AxisWhat it controlsStored inColor skinDesktop, window, taskbar, accent colors + border radiusactiveSkinIdWindow control styleMinimize / maximize / close buttonswindowControlStyle
This means you can combine any color skin with any window control style (e.g. Dracula colors + Win93 buttons).

Color Skins
Available skins

























































































IDNameModeDescriptiondefaultDefaultdarkBase FdeTheme colors, no overridesdraculaDraculadarkPurple palette — #282a36 desktop, #bd93f9 accentnordNorddarkArctic blues — #2e3440 desktop, #88c0d0 accentmonokaiMonokaidarkEditor classic — #272822 desktop, #f92672 accentmonokai-lightMonokai LightlightLight monokai variantsolarized-darkSolarized Darkdark#002b36 desktop, #2aa198 accentsolarized-lightSolarized Lightlight#fdf6e3 desktop, #2aa198 accentbreeze-darkBreeze DarkdarkKDE-inspired — #1b1b1f desktop, #3daee9 accentbreeze-lightBreeze LightlightKDE-inspired light variantwin93Win93lightWin95 teal/silver — #008080 desktop, #000080 accentwin93-darkWin93 DarkdarkWin95 dark imagined — #004040 desktop, #4040a0 accentwinxdWinXDlightXP Luna — #3a6e41 desktop, #e67822 accentwinxd-darkWinXD DarkdarkXP Luna dark imagined — #1a3a1e desktop, #c4591a accent
Architecture
All skins live in a single file:
packages/core/src/skins/index.ts   # Registry, factory, all skin definitions

Skin definition
interface FdeSkin {
  id: string;
  name: string;
  mode: &#039;light&#039; | &#039;dark&#039;;
  colors?: {
    desktop: string;
    taskbar: string;
    window: string;
    accent: string;
  };
  window?: Partial&lt;WindowTheme&gt;; // borderRadius, shadow
  taskbar?: Partial&lt;TaskbarTheme&gt;; // background
  cssVars?: Record&lt;string, string&gt;; // injected into :root
}

Note: windowControls and windowControlStyle fields exist on FdeSkin but are not used by color skins. Window control styles are managed independently via settingsStore.windowControlStyle.

createSkin factory
All skins use the internal createSkin() factory which auto-fills window.shadow based on mode and derives taskbar.background from colors.taskbar:
const nordSkin = createSkin({
  id: &#039;nord&#039;,
  name: &#039;Nord&#039;,
  mode: &#039;dark&#039;,
  colors: {
    desktop: &#039;#2e3440&#039;,
    taskbar: &#039;#242933&#039;,
    window: &#039;#3b4252&#039;,
    accent: &#039;#88c0d0&#039;,
  },
  borderRadius: &#039;12px&#039;,
  cssVars: {
    &#039;--mantine-radius-sm&#039;: &#039;8px&#039;,
    &#039;--mantine-radius-md&#039;: &#039;12px&#039;,
  },
});
Registry &amp; helpers
export const SKINS_REGISTRY: Record&lt;string, FdeSkin&gt;

export const getAllSkins = (): FdeSkin[]
export const getSkinById = (id: string | null): FdeSkin | null

Window Control Styles
Independent of color skins. Selected via settingsStore.windowControlStyle.
Available styles






























IDNameVisualclassicClassicVSCode-style icons (−, □, ×)macosmacOSTraffic lights (🔴🟡🟢)win93Win93Win95 square bevel buttons with monospace charswinxdWinXDWinXP Luna gradient buttons (yellow/green/red)
Architecture
packages/core/src/components/Shared/WindowControlStyles.tsx

export const WINDOW_CONTROL_STYLES: Record&lt;WindowControlStyle, WindowControlsOverride&gt; = {
  classic: defaultWindowControls,
  macos: macosWindowControls,
  win93: win93WindowControls,
  winxd: winXDWindowControls,
};

export function getWindowControls(style: WindowControlStyle | undefined): WindowControlsOverride;
WindowControlStyle type
// packages/core/src/interfaces/IThemeProvider.ts
export type WindowControlStyle = &#039;classic&#039; | &#039;macos&#039; | &#039;win93&#039; | &#039;winxd&#039;;

Hooks
useSkin
Returns the currently active color skin (or null for no skin):
import { useSkin } from &#039;@fde-desktop/fde-core&#039;;

function MyComponent() {
  const skin = useSkin();
  // skin.name → &#039;Dracula&#039;, skin.colors.accent → &#039;#bd93f9&#039;
}
useWindowControls
Returns the render functions for the current window control style. Used by Window.tsx to render buttons:
import { useWindowControls } from &#039;@fde-desktop/fde-core&#039;;

function WindowHeader() {
  const controls = useWindowControls();
  // controls.close({ onClick: handleClose })
  // controls.minimize({ onClick: handleMinimize })
  // controls.maximize({ onClick: handleMaximize, isMaximized })
}
Resolution is a single step: getWindowControls(settingsStore.windowControlStyle).
useWindowControlStyle
Returns the active style name:
import { useWindowControlStyle } from &#039;@fde-desktop/fde-core&#039;;

function MyComponent() {
  const style = useWindowControlStyle();
  // &#039;classic&#039; | &#039;macos&#039; | &#039;win93&#039; | &#039;winxd&#039;
}

Settings Store
interface ISettingsState {
  activeSkinId: string | null;         // null = &#039;default&#039; skin
  windowControlStyle: WindowControlStyle; // never null, defaults to &#039;classic&#039;
}

// Actions
setActiveSkin(id: string | null): void
setWindowControlStyle(style: WindowControlStyle): void
Selecting a color skin syncs the theme mode (light/dark) but does not reset windowControlStyle. Both settings are fully independent.
Auto-selection on control style change
Selecting a window control style automatically activates the canonical color skin for the current theme mode:






























Control styleDark skinLight skinclassicdefaultmonokai-lightmacosdefaultmonokai-lightwin93win93-darkwin93winxdwinxd-darkwinxd
This is implemented in setWindowControlStyle in settingsStore.ts via CONTROL_STYLE_DEFAULT_SKINS.

Settings UI
Located in Settings &gt; Skins (SkinsSettings.tsx):

SegmentedControl — selects windowControlStyle (Classic | macOS | Win93 | WinXD)
SkinCard grid — selects activeSkinId, 3-column grid with color preview

┌──────────┬──────────┬──────────┬──────────┐
│ Classic  │  macOS   │  Win93   │  WinXD   │
└──────────┴──────────┴──────────┴──────────┘

┌─────────┐ ┌─────────┐ ┌─────────┐
│ Default │ │ Dracula │ │  Nord   │
└─────────┘ └─────────┘ └─────────┘
┌─────────┐ ┌─────────┐ ┌─────────┐
│ Monokai │ │ Solar.D │ │ Solar.L │
└─────────┘ └─────────┘ └─────────┘
...


Theme Provider Integration
ThemeProvider reads the active skin and merges colors with priority:
customThemeColors &gt; theme colors &gt; skin colors &gt; base theme

CSS variables from skin.cssVars are injected into :root via useEffect.

Testing
Unit tests (Vitest)

packages/core/src/components/Shared/WindowControlStyles.test.tsx — win93 and winXD control rendering + click handlers
packages/core/tests/skins/index.test.ts — skin registry, getSkinById, getAllSkins
packages/core/tests/skins/skins.cssVars.test.ts — CSS var contracts: --color-title-bar-text, --color-surface-subtle, border radius, mode consistency
packages/core/tests/Theme/useSkin.skin.test.tsx — useSkin, useWindowControls, useWindowControlStyle hooks

Playwright integration tests
Located in tests/integration/skins-theme-sync.integration.spec.ts. These tests verify skin application via live CSS vars on document.documentElement.style — no localStorage reads, no Settings persist complications.
Key patterns used:
// Pre-load skin via localStorage before page load (bypasses Settings persist-pause)
await page.evaluate(([id, m, wcs]) =&gt; {
  localStorage.setItem(&#039;fde-desktop:settings&#039;, JSON.stringify({
    state: { activeSkinId: id, windowControlStyle: wcs, theme: { mode: m }, ... },
    version: 0,
  }));
}, [skinId, mode, windowControlStyle]);
await page.reload();

// Assert skin applied via inline CSS vars
const val = await page.evaluate(v =&gt;
  document.documentElement.style.getPropertyValue(v).trim(), &#039;--color-surface-subtle&#039;
);
expect(val).toBe(&#039;#000080&#039;);
Coverage:

Skin + theme mode synchronization (win93/winxd in light and dark mode)
setWindowControlStyle → auto-selects canonical skin
Classic control style → clears retro CSS var overrides
Theme toggle keeps skin in sync (win93 dark↔light, winxd dark↔light)
--color-title-bar-text applied per skin
Skin CSS vars applied to DOM on startup (localStorage persistence)
Skin + window control style independence

Playwright visual tests
Located in tests/visual/skins/retro-skins.visual.spec.ts. All tests use setupWithSkin() to pre-load skin state via localStorage before page load, avoiding Settings UI complications.
async function setupWithSkin(page, skinId, mode, windowControlStyle = &#039;classic&#039;) {
  // Write directly to localStorage, then reload
  // wallpaperModule: &#039;none&#039; for stable backgrounds
  // stabilizePage(): disables animations + hides clock
}
Coverage:

Title bar snapshot per skin (win93, win93-dark, winxd, winxd-dark) — maxDiffPixelRatio: 0.1
Window control styles snapshot per style via titlebar — maxDiffPixelRatio: 0.1
Full desktop snapshot per skin — maxDiffPixelRatio: 0.4 (wallpaper/clock variance)
Title bar text contrast verification: dark-bg skins → luminance &gt; 100, light-bg skins → luminance &lt; 155


Related

