concepts/wiki-system.content:
Wiki System
FDE Desktop includes an integrated wiki built with Quartz v4, a fast static site generator for Markdown content. The wiki is served as an iframe app within the desktop environment and deployed to GitHub Pages.
Architecture

Components





























ComponentDescriptionwiki/Markdown content source (committed to repo)scripts/build-wiki.tsDocker-based build script for Quartzpublic/wiki/Compiled output (NOT committed, built in CI)WikiApp.tsxIframe wrapper with scroll resetquartz.config.tsQuartz configuration (dynamic baseUrl)
Data Flow
wiki/ (Markdown) 
    ↓ Docker build (Quartz v4)
public/wiki/ (HTML)
    ↓ Vite build / CI artifact
dist/wiki/ → /wiki/* endpoint
    ↓ WikiApp iframe
Desktop UI

Building
Local Development
# Development build (baseUrl: localhost:5173/wiki)
bun run build:wiki

# Production build (baseUrl: frannunpal.github.io/wiki)
bun run build:wiki:prod
# or
WIKI_ENV=production bun run build:wiki
CI Build
The wiki is built in CI as a separate job, not committed to the repository:
bump-version → create-tag → build-wiki
                           ├→ deploy-pages
                           ├→ docker-publish  
                           └→ build-tauri


build-wiki job: Uses Docker to compile Quartz with WIKI_ENV=production
Artifact upload: wiki-{version} artifact uploaded
Consumer jobs: Download artifact before their respective builds

WikiApp Integration
The wiki is embedded via WikiApp:
// packages/core/src/components/Apps/WikiApp/WikiApp.tsx
const WikiApp: FC&lt;WikiAppProps&gt; = () =&gt; {
  const iframeRef = useRef&lt;HTMLIFrameElement&gt;(null);

  // Reset scroll position on internal navigation
  useEffect(() =&gt; {
    const iframe = iframeRef.current;
    if (!iframe) return;

    const handleLoad = () =&gt; {
      try {
        iframe.contentWindow(0, 0);
      } catch {
        // Cross-origin restricted
      }
    };

    iframe.addEventListener(&#039;load&#039;, handleLoad);
    return () =&gt; iframe.removeEventListener(&#039;load&#039;, handleLoad);
  }, []);

  return (
    &lt;iframe
      ref={iframeRef}
      src={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}wiki/index.html`}
      className={classes.wikiFrame}
    /&gt;
  );
};
CSS Configuration
/* WikiApp.module.css */
.wikiFrame {
  width: 100%;
  height: 100%;
  border: none;
  overscroll-behavior: contain;
  /* NO contain: strict — breaks scroll reset */
}
Dynamic baseUrl
Quartz needs the correct baseUrl at build time for OG metadata and internal links:
// wiki/quartz.config.ts
const config: QuartzConfig = {
  configuration: {
    // Dynamic baseUrl based on environment
    baseUrl: process.env.WIKI_ENV === &#039;production&#039; || process.env.CI === &#039;true&#039;
      ? &#039;frannunpal.github.io/wiki&#039;  // Production (no https:// prefix!)
      : &#039;localhost:5173/wiki&#039;,       // Development
    // ...
  },
};
Important: Quartz automatically adds https:// to baseUrl, so do NOT include the protocol prefix.
Build Script
The build script uses Docker to avoid installing Quartz dependencies locally:
// scripts/build-wiki.ts
// 1. Clone jackyzha0/quartz to /tmp
// 2. Build Docker image from Quartz Dockerfile
// 3. Run container with wiki/ mounted as content
// 4. Copy output to public/wiki/
Requirements:

Docker installed locally
WIKI_ENV=production for production builds

CI Workflow
# .github/workflows/release.yml
jobs:
  build-wiki:
    needs: [create-tag, bump-version]
    steps:
      - uses: actions/checkout@v5
        with:
          ref: ${{ needs.create-tag.outputs.sha }}
      - uses: oven-sh/setup-bun@v2
      - run: bun install
      - uses: docker/setup-buildx-action@v3
      - run: WIKI_ENV=production bun run build:wiki
      - uses: actions/upload-artifact@v4
        with:
          name: wiki-${{ needs.bump-version.outputs.version }}
          path: public/wiki/

  deploy-pages:
    needs: [create-tag, bump-version, build-wiki]
    steps:
      - uses: actions/download-artifact@v4
        with:
          name: wiki-${{ needs.bump-version.outputs.version }}
          path: public/wiki/
      - run: bun run build
      # ... deploy to GitHub Pages

  docker-publish:
    needs: [create-tag, bump-version, build-wiki]
    steps:
      - uses: actions/download-artifact@v4
        # ... same artifact download

  build-tauri:
    needs: [bump-version, create-tag, create-release, build-wiki]
    steps:
      - uses: actions/download-artifact@v4
        # ... same artifact download
Bug Fixes (May 2026)
SVGs Not Showing
Root cause: Hardcoded baseUrl: &#039;localhost:5173/wiki&#039; in quartz.config.ts
Fix: Dynamic baseUrl based on WIKI_ENV and CI environment variables
Scroll Position Not Resetting
Root cause: Clicking internal wiki links scrolled the iframe without resetting
Fix: Added load event listener to reset scroll position
CSS Breaking Scroll Reset
Root cause: contain: strict prevented scroll manipulation
Fix: Removed contain: strict, kept overscroll-behavior: contain
File Structure
wiki/
├── index.md              # Wiki index/catalog
├── quartz.config.ts      # Quartz config (copied to Quartz clone)
├── concepts/             # Concept documentation
│   ├── architecture.md
│   ├── hexagonal-architecture.md
│   ├── custom-apps.md
│   └── docker/
│       ├── docker-development.md
│       └── docker-production.md
├── entities/             # Entity documentation
│   ├── apps/
│   ├── stores/
│   └── infrastructure/
├── guides/               # How-to guides
├── reference/            # API reference
├── overview/             # Overview pages
└── assets/               # SVG diagrams
    ├── architecture.svg
    └── quartz-architecture.svg

public/wiki/              # Compiled output (gitignored)
├── index.html
├── 404.html
└── *.html files...

