entities/stores/settings-store.content:
Settings Store
User preferences and configuration state with persistence.
State
interface ISettingsState {
  // Theme
  theme: FdeTheme;
  themeSetManually: boolean;
  customThemeColors: CustomThemeColors | null;

  // Skins (two independent axes)
  activeSkinId: string | null; // null = &#039;default&#039; color skin
  windowControlStyle: WindowControlStyle; // never null, defaults to &#039;classic&#039;

  // Wallpaper
  wallpaper: string | null;
  wallpaperModule: string;
  wallpaperHasNoise: boolean;
  wallpaperNoiseOpacity: number;

  // Fonts
  font: string;
  fontSize: number;

  // Language
  language: SupportedLanguage; // &#039;en&#039; | &#039;es&#039;

  // Sounds
  sound: {
    enabled: boolean;
    notificationSound: string;
    customSoundUrl: string | null;
    volume: number;
  };

  // Animation
  animationDuration: number;
}
Skin Management
activeSkinId
Currently selected color skin ID. null means “default” (no color overrides):
// Available color skin IDs
[
  &#039;default&#039;,
  &#039;dracula&#039;,
  &#039;nord&#039;,
  &#039;monokai&#039;,
  &#039;monokai-light&#039;,
  &#039;solarized-dark&#039;,
  &#039;solarized-light&#039;,
  &#039;breeze-dark&#039;,
  &#039;breeze-light&#039;,
];

setActiveSkin(&#039;dracula&#039;); // activates Dracula colors
setActiveSkin(null); // back to default
Setting a skin also syncs theme.mode to the skin’s mode (light/dark).
windowControlStyle
Active window button style. Fully independent of activeSkinId — any combination is valid:
type WindowControlStyle = &#039;classic&#039; | &#039;macos&#039; | &#039;win93&#039; | &#039;winxd&#039;;

setWindowControlStyle(&#039;win93&#039;); // Win95 bevel buttons
setWindowControlStyle(&#039;classic&#039;); // VSCode-style icons

























ValueDescriptionclassicVSCode-style icons (−, □, ×) — defaultmacosTraffic lights (🔴🟡🟢)win93Windows 95 square bevel buttonswinxdWindows XP Luna gradient buttons

Priority rule (old, removed): Previously windowControlStyle could be null and deferred to the skin’s own style. This is no longer the case — the store value is always authoritative.

Theme Integration
Settings are consumed by ThemeProvider:
const skin = getSkinById(activeSkinId);
// merges: customThemeColors &gt; theme &gt; skin.colors &gt; base theme
Window controls are resolved in useWindowControls():
// Single-step resolution — no skin fallback chain
return getWindowControls(settingsStore.windowControlStyle);
Persistence
Settings are persisted to localStorage via Zustand persist middleware:
// Store key
const STORAGE_KEY = &#039;fde-desktop:settings&#039;;
Uses a “paused-aware” storage adapter to avoid flooding localStorage during rapid updates. Call pauseSettingsPersist() / resumeSettingsPersist() around bulk changes.
Actions
// Color skin
setActiveSkin: (id: string | null) =&gt; void;

// Window controls (independent of skin)
setWindowControlStyle: (style: WindowControlStyle) =&gt; void;

// Theme
setThemeMode: (mode: &#039;light&#039; | &#039;dark&#039;) =&gt; void;
toggleTheme: () =&gt; void;
setThemeAutomatic: () =&gt; void;
setCustomThemeColors: (colors: CustomThemeColors | null) =&gt; void;

// Wallpaper
setWallpaper: (url: string | null) =&gt; void;
setWallpaperModule: (module: string) =&gt; void;

// Font
setFont: (font: string) =&gt; void;
setFontSize: (size: number) =&gt; void;

// Language
setLanguage: (lang: SupportedLanguage) =&gt; void;

// Sounds
setSoundEnabled: (enabled: boolean) =&gt; void;
setSoundVolume: (volume: number) =&gt; void;
setNotificationSound: (soundId: string) =&gt; void;

// Animation
setAnimationDuration: (duration: number) =&gt; void;
