entities/window.content:
Window
Component that represents a draggable, resizable application window. Contains the app content, title bar, and window controls.
Purpose
The Window component provides:

Draggable title bar
Resizable borders
Minimize/Maximize/Close buttons
Focus management
Z-index ordering

Props
Windows are created via openWindow() from desktopStore, not directly.
Window Entity
interface WindowEntity {
  id: string;
  title: string;
  content: string;  // App ID
  x: number;
  y: number;
  width: number;
  height: number;
  minWidth?: number;
  minHeight?: number;
  isMinimized: boolean;
  isMaximized: boolean;
  icon?: string;
  fcIcon?: string;
}
Behavior

Click title bar to drag
Drag borders/corners to resize
Click to bring to front (focus)
Double-click title bar to maximize
Minimize hides to taskbar

Implementation Notes
react-rnd dragHandleClassName

CRITICAL: dragHandleClassName must receive a SINGLE class name. CSS Modules composes concatenates multiple classes, which breaks react-rnd’s drag detection.

Wrong:
// titleBar class uses composes, returns &quot;titleBar flexRow&quot;
dragHandleClassName={classes.titleBar}  // BREAKS!
Correct:
/* Create a dedicated class without composes */
.dragHandle {
  touch-action: none;
}
dragHandleClassName={classes.dragHandle}  // Single class
Traffic Light Controls
Window control buttons (macOS style) have standardized size of 14px via TRAFFIC_LIGHT_SIZE constant in WindowControlStyles.tsx.
TitleBar Sizing

min-height: 48px (not fixed height)
Uniform padding: 10px on all sides
align-items: center for vertical centering

Related

